Giggle Factory: Web Development & Video Index Workflow
1. Project Overview & Scope
Primary Domain: [https://giggle-factory.com/](https://giggle-factory.com/)

Subdirectory: /homevideos/

Core Goal: Maintain and update a responsive, SEO-optimized directory of funny home video pages and their central index.

2. File Naming & Documentation Rules
Exact Filename Comment: Every single HTML file across all web projects must include the exact file path and name as an HTML comment at the very top:

HTML
<!-- giggle-factory.com/homevideos/FILENAME.html -->
YouTube ID Integration: Individual video pages must use the exact, valid YouTube video ID for both their filename (e.g., pz9Q6TorjhM.html) and all embedded player / thumbnail sources.

Link Style: Always use absolute hard links for website navigation rather than relative links.

3. Page Layout & Technical Standards
Responsive Template: Use a clean CSS Grid layout for card containers (repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr))) and flexbox for card structures.

Branding & Assets: Maintain the signature top banner container pointing to the main site logo ([https://giggle-factory.com/images/giggle-factory-logo.png](https://giggle-factory.com/images/giggle-factory-logo.png)).

Metadata & SEO:

Include descriptive <meta name="description"> and <meta name="keywords"> tags.

Embed valid Schema.org VideoObject structured data in a <script type="application/ld+json"> block.

Dynamic Footer: Include a dynamic JavaScript fetch for shared components where applicable:

HTML
<script>
    fetch('footer.html')
        .then(response => response.text())
        .then(data => {
            document.getElementById('footer-container').innerHTML = data;
        })
        .catch(error => console.error('Error loading footer:', error));
</script>
Timestamps: Add precise last-updated timestamps including exact minutes and time zones (e.g., July 28, 2026, 8:55 PM MDT). Note: Page view counters in footers are temporarily disabled per active rules.

